    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, from `owners.POST.yml` and its 19 function classes. Every step runs inside a single `transaction` governance, so all DB writes commit once at the end (or roll back together on any thrown escalation).\n\n## Access gate (before the pipeline)\n- **`authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`** \u2014 the whole endpoint requires the `OWNER_ADMIN` role; otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException`.\n\n## Ordered validations and side-effects\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was seen before *and* its owner still exists, short-circuits with **200 OK** replaying the original owner (no creation). Otherwise takes the `proceed` flow. (`SEEN` is a static in-memory map that intentionally survives test rollback.)\n\n2. **BuildOwner** \u2014 *validation + side-effects:*\n   - `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` \u2192 **bean validation** of the request body (400 on violation; the body is bound here, the one and only `@RequestBody` binding).\n   - Maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`.\n   - If no registration date supplied, **defaults it to today**; if the supplied date is after today, throws `RegistrationDateInFutureException` (400).\n   - Publishes the built `Owner` and re-publishes the request DTO for later steps.\n\n3. **EnsureOwnerEmailNotDisposable** \u2014 *validation:* if email has a domain on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), throws `DisposableEmailException`. Absent/domain-less email passes.\n\n4. **EnsureOwnerPostcode** \u2014 *validation:* if a postcode is present it must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city with a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in range; else `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent postcode passes.\n\n5. **AdjustOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 *side-effect (mutation):* rolls the registration date forward off weekends and listed 2026 public holidays to the next business day. This adjusted date feeds later date-derived logic.\n\n6. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 *validation + side-effect:* rewrites the phone into E.164 (`+61` assumed if no `+`, dropping a leading `0`; strips spaces/dashes/brackets). Must be 8\u201315 digits; `+61` needs exactly 9 national digits, `+1` needs 10; else `InvalidTelephoneException`. Stores the E.164 value.\n\n7. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** \u2014 *validation + side-effect:* canonicalizes the address (prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, else flat `address`; trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST\u2192STREET/RD\u2192ROAD/AVE\u2192AVENUE). If no address in either form, throws `InvalidAddressException`.\n\n8. **EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold** \u2014 *side-effect + validation:* assigns the deterministic `householdId` (from last name + postcode). Then, unless `sharesHousehold=true`, rejects with `DuplicateHouseholdException` if any non-deleted owner already has that household id.\n\n9. **EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity** \u2014 *validation:* rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` if the full `IdentityKey` (normalized telephone + email + household id) exactly matches an existing non-deleted owner.\n\n10. **EnsureCityHasCapacity** \u2014 *validation:* rejects with `CityAtCapacityException` if the owner's city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) already has \u2265 50 owners.\n\n11. **EnsureDailyRegistrationCapacity** \u2014 *validation:* rejects with `DailyRegistrationLimitException` if \u2265 100 owners already share this owner's (adjusted) registration date.\n\n12. **AssignOwnerCustomerCode** \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, REGION from postcode (NSW/VIC/QLD/UNKNOWN), HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over normalized telephone + last name.\n\n13. **DeduplicateOwnerCustomerCode** \u2014 *side-effect:* if that code is already taken by another owner, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) to make it unique.\n\n14. **AssignOwnerNamesakeCount** (`countNamesakes`) \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive); runs before save so the new owner is excluded.\n\n15. **AssignOwnerHouseholdSize** (`countHousehold`) \u2014 *side-effect:* sets `householdSize` = existing owners with the same `householdId`, seeded at 1 to include this not-yet-saved owner.\n\n16. **SaveOwner** \u2014 *side-effect:* persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n\n17. **RecordIdempotencyKey** \u2014 *side-effect:* if an `Idempotency-Key` header was present, stores key \u2192 new owner id in the static `SEEN` map (enables step 1's replay).\n\n18. **AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 *side-effect:* emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membership level and number.\n\n19. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 *side-effect (response):* builds `OwnerDto`, enriches it with `bulkSignupWarning`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, and `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (suppressed when `sharesHousehold=true`), then responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n- **Validations** (can reject the request): body bean-validation (2), future date (2), disposable email (3), postcode (4), telephone format (6), missing address (7), duplicate household (8), duplicate identity (9), city capacity (10), daily capacity (11) \u2014 plus the `OWNER_ADMIN` authorization gate up front.\n- **Mutations to the owner** happen in place (`@Val` yields the stored object, not a copy): date default+roll, telephone, address, householdId, customerCode (+dedupe), namesakeCount, householdSize.\n- Any thrown checked exception is caught by the matching handler under `officefloor/escalation/` and, because it aborts the pipeline, rolls back the shared transaction.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: because `SaveOwner` (16) runs *before* `RecordIdempotencyKey` and `AuditOwnerCreated`, and all share the one transaction, the idempotency `SEEN` entry and audit log are written even though the commit only happens after step 19 \u2014 but `SEEN` is a plain static map that is *not* transactional, so a rollback after step 17 would leave a `SEEN` entry pointing at an owner id that was never committed (step 1 guards against this by re-checking the owner still exists)."
